'''Energy in Balboa''' is generated entirely by {{w|state-owned enterprise}}s under the oversight of the Ministry of Energy and Natural Resources. The country's electricity supply is approximately 11,200 MW in total capacity, generating roughly 88 TWh annually. The energy mix is diversified across nuclear, hydroelectric, thermal, and renewable sources, reflecting the government's strategy to balance industrial demand, environmental concerns, and energy security.

